invariant: INV-13
file: tcp_nonblocking_frame.c
catches: tcp_nonblocking_loop_test
reason: tcp_nonblocking_fail writes the alert record after the wipe, when the
  write key it would seal under is gone, so every handshake failure after that
  key sends its alert in the clear. bin/tcp_nonblocking_loop_test requires
  those failures to emit CH_ALERT_RECORD_LEN bytes sealed under the key the
  wipe then clears.

--- old
    size_t rec_len = alert != 0 ? alert_record(r, alert, rec) : 0;
    r->t.alert_sent = alert;
    tcp_nonblocking_wipe(r);
--- new
    r->t.alert_sent = alert;
    tcp_nonblocking_wipe(r);
    size_t rec_len = alert != 0 ? alert_record(r, alert, rec) : 0;
